<template>
<main id="main" class="wrap section legal"><LegalNav /><div class="page-head"><div><h1>Privacy policy</h1><p class="meta">Last updated {{ POLICY_DATE }}</p></div></div><div class="legal__body"><section><h2>Who we are</h2><LegalContact /><p>This policy covers the Ranked World website and desktop launcher and explains related game, bot, replay, and support data. See <NuxtLink to="/legal/business">project and contact details</NuxtLink>.</p></section><section><h2>Data we use and why</h2><ul><li>Discord ID, display name, and avatar to sign you in and identify your account. Discord login requests only the identify permission. We do not request your Discord email, messages, contacts, or password.</li><li>Your Gorilla Tag account ID, game name, account connection, scores, tags, survival time, match timestamps, and rank to operate ranked play and match history.</li><li>Party membership, invitations, friend relationships, lobby participation, and practice session results to provide those features.</li><li>Scrim, Auto Ref, and Practice movement frames and player identifiers to produce game replays. Movement can identify or distinguish players even when names are removed.</li><li>Text transcripts of voice chat in ranked codes, with the code, time, and players in the room, and short audio clips of lines that are flagged for slurs or hate speech, to moderate slurs and hate speech.</li><li>Anti-cheat data from ranked codes: your movement as the room bot receives it, per-match movement and tagging statistics, connection quality such as frame rate and ping, the custom properties your game client reports, and short video clips rendered from that movement, to detect and review cheating.</li><li>Ranked round replays: the movement, name, color, and tags of each player in a ranked round, kept for 5 days and then deleted. Players who were in the round can watch it with a membership, and staff can watch it for moderation.</li><li>Heat maps: a running count of where on the map you spend time, get tagged, and tag others in ranked rounds. Only you can see your own.</li><li>Your in-game color and the cosmetics your game reports to the room bot, used for moderation tools such as reviewing alternate accounts.</li><li>Support messages and moderation records to respond to requests, investigate abuse, and handle appeals.</li><li>Stripe customer and subscription references, plan, status, and renewal information to manage billing. Stripe receives payment details and billing information through its payment form. The website does not store your full card number or security code.</li><li>The policy version and time when you accept account, connection, or billing terms. We do not collect a birth date or an extra IP address for these acceptance records.</li><li>IP addresses and request information for network delivery, security, and rate limiting. Hosting providers can also maintain access and error logs.</li></ul></section><section><h2>What other players can see</h2><p>Your public profile can show your display name, Discord profile identifier, rank, statistics, and recent match results. Your game account ID, ban status, current room presence, and historical room codes are not included in the public profile response. Your own account can show those details. Party members and other participants can see information needed to play together.</p><p>Disconnecting stops the Discord association on your game profile. It does not erase existing records or cancel a subscription.</p></section><section><h2>Training and recordings</h2><p>We ask for separate permission to record your gameplay movement and routes in Scrims (including Auto Ref), Practice, AI Trainer, and Mirror Bot when those modes are available, and to use new replays to train and improve AI bots. We store your permission version, time, source, and any withdrawal. Accepting account or connection terms does not grant this permission.</p><p>You can withdraw permission in Settings to stop new recordings. These four modes require current permission when available. Withdrawal does not automatically delete earlier recordings or remove their influence from an existing trained model. Contact us to ask whether a recording includes you or to request access or removal.</p><p>Earlier movement recordings used for training came from official CGT scrims. Participants in those scrims were told they were being recorded to train AI bots.</p></section><section><h2>Ranked voice chat transcripts</h2><p>Voice chat in ranked codes is received by the room bot and converted to text on our own server. The audio is not saved, except a short clip of each line that is automatically flagged for slurs or hate speech. We store the text transcript, those clips, the code, when it was open, and the players who were in it.</p><p>Flagged lines and their audio clips are sent to a private staff channel, where staff review them to enforce the rules. Transcripts and clips are kept as moderation records and do not have an automatic deletion schedule. Contact us to ask for a copy or for removal.</p><p>You must agree to this before you can see or join ranked codes. Players who have not agreed are removed from ranked codes. Moderation staff are exempt while in moderation mode.</p></section><section><h2>Anti-cheat</h2><p>Room bots in ranked codes compare each player's movement with Gorilla Tag's physics and with normal player statistics. We store per-match statistics, a history of your movement statistics across matches, anti-cheat reports, and short video clips rendered from recorded movement around a suspicious moment. When a report has no clip, a room bot can record a clip of that player in a later match.</p><p>Reports and clips are sent to a private staff channel. The system does not ban anyone by itself; staff review reports before applying a ranked ban. Room bots can remove players from a code automatically for other rules, such as not being connected, being in the wrong bracket, or not agreeing to voice transcription. Rendered clips are deleted from our server after three days. Reports, statistics, and clips posted to the staff channel are kept as moderation records and do not have an automatic deletion schedule. Contact us to ask for a copy or for removal.</p><p>Room bots also record your in-game color and cosmetics. Staff tools can link Discord accounts that connected the same Gorilla Tag account to find alternate accounts, and show those accounts' color, cosmetics, and Discord avatars to staff.</p></section><section><h2>Providers and transfers</h2><p>Discord handles login and community features. Stripe handles requested payment services. Our hosting and database providers process information needed to run the service. Email providers process messages you send us. Providers can process information outside your country, including in the United States.</p><p>We serve fonts and site artwork locally. Avatar images use a restricted server proxy instead of contacting Discord from your browser. Third-party links open their own services; they are not embedded social feeds or video players.</p><p>Read <a href="https://discord.com/privacy" rel="noreferrer">Discord's Privacy policy</a> and <a href="https://stripe.com/privacy" rel="noreferrer">Stripe's Privacy policy</a>. Where transfer safeguards are legally required, those safeguards must cover the relevant provider and processing.</p></section><section><h2>Cookies and optional tracking</h2><p>The website uses necessary login and login-security cookies. No advertising, audience analytics, session replay analytics, or marketing pixel is included in this website build. Game replays are separate from website analytics. Payment technology loads only when you open checkout. See the <NuxtLink to="/legal/cookies">Cookie policy</NuxtLink>.</p><p>The website does not sell personal data or use it for targeted advertising. It does not activate sale or advertising processing when your browser sends a Global Privacy Control signal.</p></section><section><h2>Desktop launcher</h2><p>The launcher stores your selected game folder on your computer and its account session in Windows Credential Manager. The server stores a hash of the session token with your Discord account identity. Desktop sessions expire after 30 days, and browser approval requests expire after ten minutes. Signing out removes the local session and attempts to revoke it on the server.</p><p>Selecting a room writes a temporary join request in your Gorilla Tag configuration folder. Requests expire after two minutes. The helper writes local join status so the launcher can show whether the game joined. Your game folder and local join files are not uploaded by the launcher. Installing the helper copies its DLL into your existing BepInEx plugins folder.</p></section><section><h2>Retention</h2><p>Login cookies expire after seven days and login security cookies after ten minutes. Connection codes and temporary commands expire according to their service settings. Code session logs remain available while a code is open and expire 48 hours after it closes.</p><p>Account, match, practice, replay, training, billing, and moderation records do not all have automatic deletion schedules. Disconnecting is not a deletion request. Contact us for deletion or retention information. Records needed for a legal obligation or a specific dispute can require longer retention; access to those records should remain limited to that purpose.</p></section><section><h2>Your privacy choices</h2><p>Email <a :href="'mailto:' + CONTACT_EMAIL">{{ CONTACT_EMAIL }}</a> to request access, a copy, correction, deletion, restriction, or an objection to processing. Describe the request and provide the account identifier needed to locate your records. Do not send a password, full card number, or identity document unless we establish that it is necessary through a secure process.</p><p>Rights and deadlines depend on the law that applies. Where consent is the basis for an optional use, you can withdraw it without affecting earlier lawful processing. For core account and requested service functions, processing can instead be necessary to provide the service, meet legal obligations, or protect legitimate interests where the law allows. We do not treat a terms checkbox as blanket consent.</p><p>If we deny a request, you can ask for an appeal by replying to the decision. You can also complain to the <a href="https://coag.gov/file-complaint/" rel="noreferrer">Colorado Attorney General</a> or your local data protection authority. Exercising privacy rights does not by itself remove access to unrelated services.</p></section><section><h2>Young players</h2><p>Ranked World requires players to be at least 13 and to meet any higher minimum age required by local law or Discord. Minors need a parent or guardian's agreement where required. This checkbox is not age verification or verifiable parental consent. If you believe a younger child's information has been collected, contact us so we can investigate and restrict the account and processing.</p></section></div></main>
